When Cursor auto-generates a Git commit message for this repository (✨ Generate commit message) or when the agent writes a commit message here:

- Always write the commit message in Russian (subject and body).
- Use Conventional Commits prefixes in English: feat, fix, docs, chore, refactor, test, perf, ci, build, style.
- Format: `<type>: <описание на русском>` — only the type prefix, then a colon and description.
- Do NOT add a scope in parentheses after the type: no `feat(video_analysis):`, `fix(api):`, `refactor(client):`, module names, `api`/`client`/`server`, or any path segment between type and colon.

Length:

- The whole message is **1–3 complete sentences**, no more. Subject is the first sentence. Body is at most two more.
- Skip the body when one sentence already names what changed. Do not pad to three.

How to judge what happened (do this before choosing type or wording):

- Read the **diff hunks**, not the file list. Many files in one commit are usually one existing flow touched in several places, not a new product.
- Ask: did the user gain a capability that did not exist, or did something that already existed become more complete, clearer, faster, or less wrong?
- Number of files is not a new feature. Spreading one improvement across templates, tests, and config is still that improvement.
- Do not invent a subsystem, “платформенный контракт”, or architecture story unless the hunks actually introduce one. Stay at changelog / patch-note height: what a reader of git log needs to know.
- Split into two stories only when the diff contains two **unrelated** changes, not because two directories were touched. Prefer one honest sentence over two inflated ones.

Choose the type by the nature of the change, not by how impressive the file list looks:

- `feat` — only if after this commit the system can do something that previously did not exist (new screen, new command, new API, new user-facing capability).
- Existing screen, API, command, or rule that was completed, aligned, tightened, or made consistent → **not** `feat`. Use `fix` if behavior was wrong or incomplete, `refactor` if structure moved without changing behavior, `perf` / `style` / `docs` / `chore` / `test` / `ci` / `build` when that is the real story.
- Do not upgrade a polish pass or a multi-file consistency edit into `feat`.

What to write (patch-note style):

- Write as a short changelog entry for someone who will not open the diff: name the actual behavior that changed (the page, the limit, the command, the rule).
- Subject: one concrete sentence. Prefer “стало так” over “добавлена новая система”.
- Body: only an anchor the subject cannot hold (`TIME_ZONE`, `/upload/`, `--cleanup-users`) or a second real consequence. Not a file dump.
- Docs and Cursor rules: say what the instruction became, not that “правила обновлены”.
- Do not copy the vague style of older auto-generated commits (`Добавлены новые настройки…`, `Добавлены улучшения…`, `Обновлены правила…`). Name what improved.
- Do not dump files. Do not write filler (`улучшения`, `доработки`, `рефакторинг` without saying what already existed and what is now different).

Language: plain Russian, full sentences. No Anglicisms when a Russian word exists. Keep identifiers as in the diff.

Good (one existing flow, several files, not a new feature):
```
refactor: Выбор даты на страницах анализа видео идёт через общий DatePicker.

Фильтр по дате загрузки и поле в форме больше не расходятся по разным виджетам.
```

Good (real new capability):
```
feat: Загрузки обычного пользователя и администратора больше не делят один лимит.

Частоту считают одно место для media_api и nginx. Зона nginx на /upload/ берёт потолок администратора.
```

Good (small change stays one sentence):
```
fix: На странице анализа видео фильтр учитывает дату загрузки, а не только дату съёмки.
```

Bad (multi-file improvement inflated to a new feature):
```
feat: Добавлена новая система фильтрации и выбора даты на страницах анализа видео.
```

Bad (architecture story the hunks do not support):
```
feat: Единый контракт лимитов загрузки вынесен в платформенный слой media_api и nginx.
```

Bad (file-scale: counts files, misses what changed):
```
feat: Обновлены render_common.py, шаблоны nginx, профили безопасности и тесты загрузки.
```

Bad (inventory of keys):
```
feat: Добавлены MEDIA_API_UPLOAD_RATE_ADMIN, upload_rate.py и правки profiles.yaml.
```

Bad (empty label):
```
feat: Обновление интерфейса страниц анализа видео с новым макетом и стилями.
```
